_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 97
---
order: 97
---
short_label: X.97
---
statement: The square on an apotome of a medial straight line applied to a rational straight line produces as breadth a first apotome.
---
proof:

Let *AB* be an apotome, and *CD* rational, and to *CD* let there be applied *CE* equal to the square on *AB* and producing *CF* as breadth.

I say that *CF* is a first apotome.

Let *BG* be the annex to *AB*. Then *AG* and *GB* are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. [!just X.73]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="370" height="170" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.97 diagram" src="propX97.gif"/></noscript>
